      {
        "ballot_id": "B024",
        "laureates": [
          "Jens Juul Holst",
          "Svetlana Mojsov",
          "Daniel J. Drucker"
        ],
        "citation": "for discoveries of GLP-1 physiology that enabled transformative treatments for diabetes and obesity"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B047",
    "B017"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "B024 most convincingly unites a fundamental endocrine discovery with mature, exceptionally broad therapeutic consequences. Holst, Mojsov, and Drucker provide a coherent attribution spanning identification and biological understanding of the active peptide and its physiological and translational development. The mechanism and long-term clinical importance in diabetes and obesity are well established.",
    "case_against": "Its chief weakness is attribution: clinically successful medicines required important additional drug-development work, and the boundary between foundational GLP-1 biology and later therapeutic optimization must be drawn carefully.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "linnarsson-sten",
        "point": "Linnarsson argues that Lotte Bjerre Knudsen should represent crucial translation into durable GLP-1 therapeutic agents.",
        "response": "That is a serious attribution case and reinforces the importance of translational development. I nevertheless retain Drucker because the proposed achievement is best framed as GLP-1 physiology and its therapeutic enablement, for which his linked biological and translational contributions keep the citation focused on the discovery rather than on a particular drug-development program."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "el-manira-abdel",
        "point": "El Manira ranks optogenetics first because it created an exceptionally powerful causal method for studying specified cells and circuits.",
        "response": "I agree that B002 is a landmark methodological and physiological advance, but its essential contributions extend across several stages and exceed a readily defensible three-person allocation. B024 presently has both more compact attribution and more direct, mature medical consequence."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "wahren-herlenius-marie",
        "point": "Wahren-Herlenius emphasizes the preventive, global-health significance and mature real-world benefit of HPV virus-like-particle vaccines.",
        "response": "B047 is an especially strong alternative: its preventive effect against infection-associated cancer is compelling and its three-person attribution is plausible. I place B024 ahead because the endocrine discovery-to-therapy connection has transformed care across two highly prevalent metabolic conditions, while recognizing that B047 warrants close comparative consideration."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the most historically defensible third laureate for B024 is Daniel J. Drucker or Lotte Bjerre Knudsen.",
      "How narrowly the prize citation should delimit foundational GLP-1 physiology from subsequent pharmaceutical development."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile."
  }
}
